:: Carter Hero's Weakness Part 4 [nobr]

/* Intro */
<<set $Minutes += 10>>
The two of you move into <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Callum</span>’s room, dark and mysterious like the rest of the house. Or, it would be, if not for the lava lamp and LED lights on his desk. When you point out the rather weird choice of décor, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> just shrugs, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“He tried to do this streaming thing after a friend talked him into it, but I’m not sure how well it worked. The lights are pretty cool though. Adds a level of mystique to the room!”</span> You nod before getting back in character, creeping around to the center of the room and searching for any hidden traps or danger. <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Looks clear, he must not know we are here.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> explains, <span style="color:LightGreen">once again in his deep, heroic voice that you can’t help but smile at,</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“So we should be in the clear to look around. I feel like the device will be pretty obvious, so look for something that seems out of place. I’ll check this side of the room; you get that side!”</span> You nod, walking over towards <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Callum</span>’s desk to begin to search. <span style="color:Yellow">You feel a little strange about going through <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>’s brother’s stuff but figure it can’t be all bad if <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> instructed you to do it.</span> <br>

    <<set _ad to [
            {
                Name: "Player",
                State: {
                    Mouth: "Smirk",
                    Eyes: "Tired",
                },
                },
            {
                Name: "Carter",
                State: {
                    Outfit: "Everyday",
                    Mouth: "Happy",
                },
            },
        ]>>
    <<ad _ad>>

The device <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> wants you to find is pretty easy to spot, a weird, out of place Blockz creation sitting in the corner of the desk with a piece of scotch tape on it with the words <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“MIND CONTROL DEVICE”</span> labeled on it. <span style="color:Pink">It’s rather cute, even if it looks very haphazardly put together and not at all hidden. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> must have been in a rush, overly excited when he was setting up this game for the two of you.</span> You pretend to keep looking for a moment, not wanting the hunt to end too quickly, when you get an interesting idea. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Callum</span>’s dirty laundry basket is right next to his desk, <span style="color:Pink">and you just so happen to see a sweaty looking jockstrap sitting at the top of it.</span> Makes sense, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Callum</span> looks pretty big and must play sports. <span style="color:Pink">You could pretend that you think this is the device, toss it to <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> just to see his reaction.</span> <br>
<br>
But then you spot something else in one of the drawers: a framed photo. You only look at it briefly, stopping in your tracks as you see who is in the photo. <span style="color:Yellow">It appears to be a photo of all three of the brothers, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Callum</span>, and <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Connor</span>. It’s from when they were younger, as you believe the twins look about 2-3 years old from the glance you got. You could inspect it more closely, but <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> would no doubt notice and may get upset at you looking at something like that.</span> <br>
<br>

<div id="choice">
    <<link "Grab the Mind Control Device<br>">>
    <<replace "#choice">>
        You grab the strange Blockz build and whisper-ask <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> if this is it, <span style="color:LightGreen">pointing to the scotch tape label on it with a smirk. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> blushes, nodding with a smile.</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I guess A.U. didn’t have much time to set up, since he expected us here EARLIER than we arrived.”</span> You chuckle, moving over to <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> and asking how this thing works. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“From what I can tell, it’s like some sort of laser beam. Once you hit the target, they are under mind control until the device is reversed or destroyed.”</span> With that in mind, you ask <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> if the two of you should just destroy the device and move on. <br>
        <br>
        <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Hmm…”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> thinks it over for a moment, before shaking his head, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“No, we should try to retrieve it in one piece. I don’t agree with such a device, but it is our job to return it to its owner if we can. We can discuss the morales of mind-control of any fashion after. Come on, let’s get moving before we are spotted.”</span> <br>
        <<needChange "Fun" 10>>
        <br>
        [[Continue|Carter Hero's Weakness Part 5]]<br>
    <</replace>>
    <</link>>
    <<link "Grab the jockstrap<br>">>
    <<replace "#choice">>
        <span style="color:Pink">You grab the jockstrap, still feeling the slight moistness of it in your palms, as you crumble it in your hand and hide it behind your back.</span> You then whistle to <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>, telling him you found something. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Really? What did you-?”</span> <span style="color:Pink">You wait until <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>’s mouth is open before tossing the jockstrap straight at his face. The pouch, right where his older brother’s sweaty balls would sit, goes directly into his mouth. You couldn’t have asked for better aim.</span> <br>

            <<set _ad to [
                    {
                        Name: "Player",
                        State: {
                            Mouth: "Smirk",
                            Eyes: "Tired",
                            Blush: 1,
                        },
                        },
                    {
                        Name: "Carter",
                        State: {
                            Outfit: "Everyday",
                            Mouth: "Frown",
                            Blush: 2,
                        },
                    },
                ]>>
            <<ad _ad>>

        <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Ack!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> <span style="color:Pink">gags and spits, no doubt tasting the salty substance of his older brother.</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“What the heck!? That’s disgusting, you-! Are you sure you aren’t the villain!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> tosses the jockstrap back at you, though you manage to duck underneath it, the well-worn underwear landing on his desk, dangling lewdly from the corner. You chuckle at <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>, asking with faux ignorance if that wasn’t it. He glares at you in annoyance. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“One of these days, I’m going to have my dark hero arc and then have my revenge!”</span> <br>
        <br>
        You laugh and tease <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> about his so-called dark hero arc’ as you continue searching. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> eventually gives up trying to direct you towards it and points out the Blockz creation himself, pointing to the scotch tape label. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“This must be it! Come on, we gotta get this back to the lab before we are spotted. It has the power to put anyone under a villain’s control. I’d vote we just break it, but we have to do the right thing and bring it back to its proper owner. Come on!”</span> <span style="color:LightGreen">You follow <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> along, smile on your face as you crouch low back in the hallway towards his bedroom.</span> <br>
        <<needChange "Fun" 10>>
        <br>
        [[Continue|Carter Hero's Weakness Part 5]]<br>
    <</replace>>
    <</link>>
    <<link "Grab the photo<br>">>
    <<replace "#choice">>
        You pick up the photo from the drawer, trying to be careful as you examine it more closely. <span style="color:LightGreen">As you expected, it is of <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Callum</span>, and <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Connor</span>. He really does look exactly like <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>, with the only difference being their attire. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> is most likely the one in the Ultraman Diaper while <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Connor</span> rocks an Owlman one that could even make your brother consider it.</span> Their smiles are identical though, both overjoyed as they cuddle with their big brother. You’d wager they are both about two years old, in that odd spot between toddlers and babies. <span style="color:LightGreen">It’s frankly adorable.</span> <br>

            <<set _ad to [
                    {
                        Name: "Player",
                        State: {
                            Mouth: "Frown",
                        },
                        },
                    {
                        Name: "Carter",
                        State: {
                            Outfit: "Everyday",
                            Mouth: "Frown",
                            Blush: 2,
                        },
                    },
                ]>>
            <<ad _ad>>

        <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Hey, what did you-?”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> <span style="color:Yellow">freezes as he sees what’s in your hand, frowning as his eyes linger on it.</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“O- oh…”</span> You quickly apologize, not wanting to upset <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>, and try to explain you just found it and were curious. You weren’t going to mention it to him since- <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“It’s fine, really. Let’s just…”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> looks to the left, spotting the Blockz creation on the table. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“This… must be it. Come on, we should get back. This thing is bad news, can take over hero’s minds and…”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> <span style="color:Yellow">pauses, taking a deep breath before smiling and trying to return to his normal self.</span> <br>
        <br>
        <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“We have to get this back to the owner, even if I don’t agree with anyone having mind control powers. Come on!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> grabs you by the hand and leads you back into the hallway, leaving the photo back where you found it. <span style="color:Yellow">Judging by everything you’ve seen, you’re starting to gather the twins had a falling out with each other, or something of the sort. The photo must have reminded him of happier times. You can’t help but wonder if there is anything you can do to help.</span> <br>
        <<needChange "Fun" 10>>
        <br>
        [[Continue|Carter Hero's Weakness Part 5]]<br>
    <</replace>>
    <</link>>
</div>